## Ab Natural Join Samjhate Hain 🔥

**T1(A,B)** aur **T2(B,C)** ka join matlab — **B column common hai**, uspe match karna hai.

---

### STEP 1 - MAP Phase

**Idea:** Dono tables se B ko **key** banao, aur value mein — *kis table se aaya* ye bhi batao!

**T1 se mapping:**
```
b1 → ("T1", a1)
b1 → ("T1", a2)
b2 → ("T1", a3)
b3 → ("T1", a4)
```

**T2 se mapping:**
```
b2 → ("T2", c1)
b2 → ("T2", c2)
b3 → ("T2", c3)
```

---

### STEP 2 - SHUFFLE Phase

Same B value wale sab ek reducer ke paas aate hain:

```
b1 → [ ("T1",a1), ("T1",a2) ]           ← T2 se koi nahi, join nahi hoga
b2 → [ ("T1",a3), ("T2",c1), ("T2",c2) ]
b3 → [ ("T1",a4), ("T2",c3) ]
```

---

### STEP 3 - REDUCE Phase

**Logic:** T1 wali values aur T2 wali values ka **cross-product** banao

**b2 ke liye:**
```
T1 list = [a3]
T2 list = [c1, c2]

Cross product:
a3 × c1 → (a3, b2, c1) ✅
a3 × c2 → (a3, b2, c2) ✅
```

**b3 ke liye:**
```
T1 list = [a4]
T2 list = [c3]

Cross product:
a4 × c3 → (a4, b3, c3) ✅
```

**b1 ke liye:**
```
T1 list = [a1, a2]
T2 list = []  ← khaali hai!

Koi output nahi ❌ (natural join mein unmatched rows nahi aate)
```

---

### Final Output ✅

| A | B | C |
|---|---|---|
| a3 | b2 | c1 |
| a3 | b2 | c2 |
| a4 | b3 | c3 |

---

## Ek Line Mein Yaad Rakh 🧠

> **MAP** = B ko key banao, table ka naam value mein daalo
> **REDUCE** = T1 ki list × T2 ki list = Join result

